@lang en
IMPORT `cstd-ch2-benefits`

-- Tests for Chapter 1 (Articles 1 to 11). Every expected value was worked out by hand from
-- the words and figures of the clause cited, before it was run; none was copied from an
-- evaluation. Where a value depends on a fork, the fork is named. A failing assertion here is
-- a finding, never a value to edit.

§ `Tests — Chapter 1`

§§ `1.6 Tuổi, 1.7 dates, 1.8 and 1.9 terms`

-- Born 15 March 1990. Completed years counts the birthday on its day: 40 on 15 March 2030.
#ASSERT `the completed years from` (YMD 1990 3 15) `to` (YMD 2030 3 15) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `the completed years from` (YMD 1990 3 15) `to` (YMD 2030 3 14) EQUALS 39
-- 1.6, fork F-1.6a: Tuổi on an anchor day counts only birthdays BEFORE it.
#ASSERT `the Tuổi on the anchor day` (YMD 2030 3 15) `of someone born` (YMD 1990 3 15) EQUALS 39
#ASSERT `the Tuổi on the anchor day` (YMD 2030 3 16) `of someone born` (YMD 1990 3 15) EQUALS 40

-- 1.7.3: an effective date of 29 February 2024; no 29 February in 2025, so the last day of
-- that month, 28 February 2025; 2028 has one again.
`C-leap` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2024 2 29) `for an insured born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT `the policy anniversary` 1 `of` `C-leap` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT `the policy anniversary` 4 `of` `C-leap` EQUALS YMD 2028 2 29

-- 1.7.4 policy years of a contract effective 1 June 2020.
`C-june` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2020 6 1) `for an insured born` (YMD 1985 9 10) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT `the policy year of` `C-june` `in which falls` (YMD 2020 6 1) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the policy year of` `C-june` `in which falls` (YMD 2021 5 31) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the policy year of` `C-june` `in which falls` (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS 2

-- 1.6: born 10 September 1985; Tuổi at the effective date 1 June 2020 is 34; it stays 34 for
-- the whole first policy year, though the insured turns 35 in September; 35 from 1 June 2021.
#ASSERT `the insured's Tuổi under` `C-june` `on` (YMD 2020 12 1) EQUALS 34
#ASSERT `the insured's Tuổi under` `C-june` `on` (YMD 2021 6 1) EQUALS 35

-- 1.8: the term ends at the anniversary at which the insured reaches 99 Tuổi: 34 + 65 = 99,
-- the 65th anniversary, 1 June 2085. 1.9: the premium term ends at the 15th, 1 June 2035.
#ASSERT `the maturity date of` `C-june` EQUALS YMD 2085 6 1
#ASSERT `the end of the premium term of` `C-june` EQUALS YMD 2035 6 1

§§ `1.2 and 1.3 Who may be policyholder and insured`

-- 1.2: an individual born 2 June 2008 is 17 on 1 June 2026 and 18 on 2 June 2026.
#ASSERT NOT (`1.2 — may be the policyholder on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `:` (`an individual` (YMD 2008 6 2) TRUE TRUE))
#ASSERT `1.2 — may be the policyholder on` (YMD 2026 6 2) `:` (`an individual` (YMD 2008 6 2) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`1.2 — may be the policyholder on` (YMD 2026 6 2) `:` (`an individual` (YMD 2008 6 2) FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `1.2 — may be the policyholder on` (YMD 2026 6 2) `:` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`1.2 — may be the policyholder on` (YMD 2026 6 2) `:` (`an organisation` FALSE FALSE))

-- 1.3: from one month old (born 15 January 2026: one month on 15 February 2026) to 65 Tuổi
-- (born 1 July 1960: Tuổi 65 on 1 July 2026, 66 on 2 July 2026), counted at the application.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An application`
`an application on` d MEANS `An application` WITH
    `date of the application`  IS d
    `the insured alive`        IS TRUE
    `an insurable relationship between the policyholder and the insured` IS TRUE
    `the insured present in Vietnam` IS TRUE
    `the insured a minor`      IS FALSE
    `written consent given by` IS `the insured`
`C-baby` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2026 3 1) `for an insured born` (YMD 2026 1 15) `of sex` `female`
`C-65`   MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2026 8 1) `for an insured born` (YMD 1960 7 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT NOT (`1.3 — the insured may be insured under` `C-baby` `on the application` (`an application on` (YMD 2026 2 14)))
#ASSERT `1.3 — the insured may be insured under` `C-baby` `on the application` (`an application on` (YMD 2026 2 15))
#ASSERT `1.3 — the insured may be insured under` `C-65` `on the application` (`an application on` (YMD 2026 7 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`1.3 — the insured may be insured under` `C-65` `on the application` (`an application on` (YMD 2026 7 2)))

§§ `1.15 to 1.19`

-- 1.15: half the table value from a late-stage approval (1 January 2030) until the coupon
-- arises (1 January 2040); the full value before and after, and with no approval.
#ASSERT `1.15 — the cash value on` (YMD 2035 1 1) `from the table value` 100000000 `, the late-stage benefit approved on` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) `and the coupon arising on` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS 50000000
#ASSERT `1.15 — the cash value on` (YMD 2029 12 31) `from the table value` 100000000 `, the late-stage benefit approved on` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) `and the coupon arising on` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `1.15 — the cash value on` (YMD 2040 1 1) `from the table value` 100000000 `, the late-stage benefit approved on` (JUST (YMD 2030 1 1)) `and the coupon arising on` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS 100000000
#ASSERT `1.15 — the cash value on` (YMD 2035 1 1) `from the table value` 100000000 `, the late-stage benefit approved on` NOTHING `and the coupon arising on` (YMD 2040 1 1) EQUALS 100000000

-- 1.16: 100 + 5 + 10 + 2 - 20 = 97 (millions).
#ASSERT `1.16 — the surrender value from` 100 `,` 5 `,` 10 `,` 2 `less` 20 EQUALS 97

-- 1.17: injury 90 days after the event is within the definition; 91 days is not; nor is an
-- event that is not the sole cause.
#ASSERT `1.17 — an Accident:` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, injuring on` (YMD 2026 4 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`1.17 — an Accident:` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, injuring on` (YMD 2026 4 2)))
#ASSERT NOT (`1.17 — an Accident:` (`An accident` WITH `date of the event` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `an objective event of a sudden external force or object on the body` IS TRUE, `the direct and sole cause, unrelated to any other cause` IS FALSE, `date of the injury or death` IS YMD 2026 1 2))

-- 1.19: issued 10 January 2026; examined on 9 January is pre-existing, on 10 January not;
-- after a reinstatement on 1 March 2027, examined on 28 February 2027 is pre-existing.
`C-1-19`  MEANS `a contract issued` (YMD 2026 1 10) `effective` (YMD 2026 1 10) `reinstated` NOTHING `with a premium term` `to the 12th policy anniversary` `for an insured born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `of sex` `male`
`C-1-19r` MEANS `a contract issued` (YMD 2026 1 10) `effective` (YMD 2026 1 10) `reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1)) `with a premium term` `to the 12th policy anniversary` `for an insured born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT `1.19 — a pre-existing condition under` `C-1-19` `:` (`a diagnosis of` `stroke` `on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `measuring` EMPTY `, first examined` (YMD 2026 1 9) `, declared` FALSE `, self-harm` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, nuclear` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`1.19 — a pre-existing condition under` `C-1-19` `:` (`a diagnosis of` `stroke` `on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `measuring` EMPTY `, first examined` (YMD 2026 1 10) `, declared` FALSE `, self-harm` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, nuclear` FALSE))
#ASSERT `1.19 — a pre-existing condition under` `C-1-19r` `:` (`a diagnosis of` `stroke` `on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `measuring` EMPTY `, first examined` (YMD 2027 2 28) `, declared` FALSE `, self-harm` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, nuclear` FALSE)

§§ `Article 2`

GIVEN who   IS A `A person who may give written consent`
      minor IS A BOOLEAN
      rel   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An application`
`an application with consent by` who `, minor` minor `, relationship` rel MEANS `An application` WITH
    `date of the application`  IS YMD 2026 1 1
    `the insured alive`        IS TRUE
    `an insurable relationship between the policyholder and the insured` IS rel
    `the insured present in Vietnam` IS TRUE
    `the insured a minor`      IS minor
    `written consent given by` IS who
#ASSERT NOT (`2.3 — the contract has no effect from the start:` (`an application with consent by` `the insured` `, minor` FALSE `, relationship` TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`2.3 — the contract has no effect from the start:` (`an application with consent by` `a parent or lawful guardian of the insured` `, minor` TRUE `, relationship` TRUE))
#ASSERT `2.3 — the contract has no effect from the start:` (`an application with consent by` `a parent or lawful guardian of the insured` `, minor` FALSE `, relationship` TRUE)
#ASSERT `2.3 — the contract has no effect from the start:` (`an application with consent by` `nobody` `, minor` FALSE `, relationship` TRUE)
#ASSERT `2.3 — the contract has no effect from the start:` (`an application with consent by` `the insured` `, minor` FALSE `, relationship` FALSE)
-- Refund: 10 - 3 - 1 = 6; and nothing clawed back when the deductions exceed the premiums.
#ASSERT `2.3 — the refund of` 10000000 `less` 3000000 `and` 1000000 EQUALS 6000000
#ASSERT `2.3 — the refund of` 2000000 `less` 3000000 `and` 1000000 EQUALS 0

§§ `Article 3 — temporary cover`

-- Stamped 1 March 2026; issued 20 March 2026; death 10 March by Accident (event 9 March).
GIVEN death  IS A DATE
      event  IS A DATE
      acc    IS A MAYBE `An accident`
      sui    IS A BOOLEAN
      crime  IS A MAYBE `A criminal act`
      sa     IS A NUMBER
      prem   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A death during temporary cover`
`a temporary-cover death on` death `, event` event `, accident` acc `, suicide` sui `, crime` crime `, pending sum insured` sa `, premiums` prem MEANS
    `A death during temporary cover` WITH
        `date the Company stamped receipt of the complete application and the full provisional premium` IS YMD 2026 3 1
        `date of the event leading to the death`               IS event
        `date of death`                                        IS death
        `date the contract was issued, or postponement or refusal was notified` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)
        `the accident causing it`                              IS acc
        `suicide, whether sane or insane`                      IS sui
        `a criminal act causing it`                            IS crime
        `total sum insured of the main products on all pending applications` IS sa
        `total premiums paid on all pending applications`      IS prem
        `medical and underwriting costs`                       IS 1000000

`the March accident` MEANS JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, injuring on` (YMD 2026 3 10))

-- 3.1: the lesser of the pending sum insured and 200 million.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 150000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 150000000
-- 3.1: premiums of exactly 200 million do not exceed it; one dong more, and only the premiums
-- come back.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 200000000) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 200000001) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 200000001
-- 3.2(a) suicide; (b) a criminal act of the policyholder, and of the insured even if
-- unintentional; near miss: a criminal act of someone else; (c) the event before the stamp.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` NOTHING `, suicide` TRUE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 19000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` (JUST (`A criminal act` OF `the policyholder in person`, FALSE)) `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 19000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` (JUST (`A criminal act` OF `the insured himself or herself`, TRUE)) `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 19000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` (JUST (`A criminal act` OF `someone else`, FALSE)) `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200000000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 2 28) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `a refund of the premiums paid` 19000000
-- 3.1, the period: a death on the issue day is outside it (fork F-3a), as is one before the stamp.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 20) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `no answer under Article 3: the death fell outside the temporary cover period`
#ASSERT `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 19) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` `the March accident` `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200000000
-- A death by illness: Article 3 does not say (finding X-13).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3 — the answer on` (`a temporary-cover death on` (YMD 2026 3 10) `, event` (YMD 2026 3 9) `, accident` NOTHING `, suicide` FALSE `, crime` NOTHING `, pending sum insured` 500000000 `, premiums` 20000000) BECAUSE "Article 3 does not say what follows a death during temporary cover that is neither by Accident nor by an excluded cause"

§§ `Article 4 — the free-look period`

-- Received 1 May 2026: the 21st day after is 22 May 2026.
#ASSERT `4 — the last day to refuse the contract received on` (YMD 2026 5 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 5 22
#ASSERT `4 — the refund of` 15000000 `less` 1000000 `and` 0 EQUALS 14000000
#ASSERT REFUSED `4 — the refund of` 1000000 `less` 2000000 `and` 0 BECAUSE "Article 4 does not say what follows when the deductions exceed the premium paid"
-- The right used on day 21 leaves the Company's duty to refund standing; unused, it lapses.
#TRACE `4 — the policyholder's right to refuse the contract` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Policyholder` DOES `send written notice refusing the contract, with the premium receipts and the contract` AT 21
#TRACE `4 — the policyholder's right to refuse the contract` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 22)

§§ `Articles 5 and 6`

#ASSERT `5.1 — the return on termination for the Company's false information, of` 30000000 `less` 5000000 EQUALS 25000000
#ASSERT `5.2 — the transfer is permitted:` TRUE `,` FALSE
#ASSERT `5.2 — the transfer is permitted:` FALSE `,` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`5.2 — the transfer is permitted:` FALSE `,` FALSE)
#TRACE `5.2 — the Company's duty of confidentiality` FALSE `,` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Company` DOES `transfer personal information to a third party` AT 5

GIVEN i IS A BOOLEAN
      w IS A BOOLEAN
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A BOOLEAN
      p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A breach of the duty to disclose`
`a breach` i w a r p MEANS `A breach of the duty to disclose` OF i, w, a, r, p
-- 6.2: intentional, would not have accepted, related to the event: terminate, refuse, return.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the consequence of` (`a breach` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `The consequence of a breach of the duty to disclose` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
-- 6.2: intentional, not related, not about health, occupation or income: terminate, return,
-- but the benefit is not refused by 6.2.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the consequence of` (`a breach` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `The consequence of a breach of the duty to disclose` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
-- 6.2(ii): about a pre-existing condition.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the consequence of` (`a breach` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `The consequence of a breach of the duty to disclose` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
-- 6.3: did not affect the decision: the benefit is paid; an additional premium may be charged.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — the consequence of` (`a breach` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `The consequence of a breach of the duty to disclose` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
-- Neither: not intentional but affected the decision (finding X-14).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 6 — the consequence of` (`a breach` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "Article 6 does not provide for a breach that was not intentional but affected the decision to accept"
-- 6.2, fraud: of 50 million approved and unpaid, only the 3 million of dividends and interest.
#ASSERT `6.2 — what remains payable on discovering fraud, of` 50000000 `with` 3000000 EQUALS 3000000

§§ `Articles 7 and 8`

-- 7.1(a): 10 paid against 12.5 due: the sum insured of 1 billion becomes 800 million (fork F-7a).
#ASSERT `7.1 — the adjustment for` 1000000000 `with` 10000000 `paid against` 12500000 EQUALS `the sum insured is reduced to` 800000000
#ASSERT `7.1 — the adjustment for` 1000000000 `with` 12000000 `paid against` 10000000 EQUALS `the excess premium is refunded` 2000000
#ASSERT `7.1 — the adjustment for` 1000000000 `with` 10000000 `paid against` 10000000 EQUALS `no adjustment`
-- 7.2: the greater of 5 and 20 - 3 - 1 = 16; of 30 and 16; and nothing when both are below 0.
#ASSERT `the greater of the surrender value` 5000000 `and the premiums` 20000000 `less` 3000000 `and` 1000000 EQUALS 16000000
#ASSERT `the greater of the surrender value` 30000000 `and the premiums` 20000000 `less` 3000000 `and` 1000000 EQUALS 30000000
#ASSERT `the greater of the surrender value` 0 `and the premiums` 2000000 `less` 3000000 `and` 1000000 EQUALS 0

-- 8: issued 15 January 2024: 24 months run on 15 January 2026; after a reinstatement on 1 June
-- 2025, on 1 June 2027. Age and sex are never protected.
`C-8`  MEANS `a contract issued` (YMD 2024 1 15) `effective` (YMD 2024 1 15) `reinstated` NOTHING `with a premium term` `to the 12th policy anniversary` `for an insured born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `of sex` `male`
`C-8r` MEANS `a contract issued` (YMD 2024 1 15) `effective` (YMD 2024 1 15) `reinstated` (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) `with a premium term` `to the 12th policy anniversary` `for an insured born` (YMD 1990 1 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT NOT (`8 — on` (YMD 2026 1 14) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8` `for a misstatement` `an inaccurate statement or an omission otherwise`)
#ASSERT `8 — on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8` `for a misstatement` `an inaccurate statement or an omission otherwise`
#ASSERT NOT (`8 — on` (YMD 2027 5 31) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8r` `for a misstatement` `an inaccurate statement or an omission otherwise`)
#ASSERT `8 — on` (YMD 2027 6 1) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8r` `for a misstatement` `an inaccurate statement or an omission otherwise`
#ASSERT NOT (`8 — on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8` `for a misstatement` `of age or sex, under Article 7`)
#ASSERT NOT (`8 — on` (YMD 2030 1 1) `the contract can no longer be voided under` `C-8` `for a misstatement` `intentional, of what would have led the Company to postpone or refuse cover`)

§§ `Articles 9 to 11`

#ASSERT `9 — a payment by the Company conforms:` TRUE `,` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`9 — a payment by the Company conforms:` TRUE `,` FALSE)

-- 10.1: insured born 1 June 2005, contract effective 1 January 2020. On 1 March 2023 the
-- Tuổi is 17 (fixed on 1 January 2023); on 1 March 2024 it is 18.
`C-10` MEANS `a contract effective` (YMD 2020 1 1) `for an insured born` (YMD 2005 6 1) `of sex` `male`
#ASSERT `10.1 — the successor to the policyholder of` `C-10` `on` (YMD 2023 3 1) `,` TRUE EQUALS `the insured's guardian, on applying and with the Company's approval`
#ASSERT `10.1 — the successor to the policyholder of` `C-10` `on` (YMD 2024 3 1) `,` TRUE EQUALS `the insured, with the Company's approval`
#ASSERT `10.1 — the successor to the policyholder of` `C-10` `on` (YMD 2024 3 1) `,` FALSE EQUALS `no successor, the insured not meeting the policyholder conditions`

-- 10.2: three beneficiaries, no shares stated, all alive: a third each; the second dead: a
-- half each to the others; stated shares 0.5 / 0.3 / 0.2 with the second dead: 0.65 / 0 /
-- 0.35; nobody surviving: the policyholder; an organisation with no beneficiary: the
-- insured's heirs; shares stated for some only: not provided for.
`b-alive` MEANS `A beneficiary` OF FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING
`b-dead`  MEANS `A beneficiary` OF FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` (LIST `b-alive`, `b-alive`, `b-alive`) EQUALS `the beneficiaries, in these shares` (LIST 1/3, 1/3, 1/3)
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` (LIST `b-alive`, `b-dead`, `b-alive`) EQUALS `the beneficiaries, in these shares` (LIST 1/2, 0, 1/2)
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` (LIST (`A beneficiary` OF FALSE, TRUE, JUST 0.5), (`A beneficiary` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST 0.3), (`A beneficiary` OF FALSE, TRUE, JUST 0.2)) EQUALS `the beneficiaries, in these shares` (LIST 0.65, 0, 0.35)
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` (LIST `b-dead`, `b-dead`) EQUALS `the policyholder or the policyholder's lawful heirs`
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE) `and the beneficiaries` EMPTY EQUALS `the heirs of the insured`
#ASSERT `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` EMPTY EQUALS `the policyholder or the policyholder's lawful heirs`
#ASSERT REFUSED `10.2 — the recipients of the death benefit, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `and the beneficiaries` (LIST (`A beneficiary` OF FALSE, TRUE, JUST 0.5), `b-alive`) BECAUSE "Article 10.2 does not say how to share where some shares are stated and others are not"
-- 10.2(b), (e)(i): payees.
#ASSERT `10.2 — the payee, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder` `, of` `a critical illness benefit` EQUALS `the policyholder`
#ASSERT `10.2 — the payee, with the policyholder` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE) `, of` `a critical illness benefit` EQUALS `the insured`
#ASSERT `10.2 — the payee, with the policyholder` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE) `, of` `a dividend` EQUALS `the policyholder`
#ASSERT `10.2 — the payee, with the policyholder` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE) `, of` `the death benefit` EQUALS `the beneficiaries under 10.2`
#ASSERT `10.2 — changing the beneficiary needs the insured's consent, with the policyholder` (`an organisation` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`10.2 — changing the beneficiary needs the insured's consent, with the policyholder` `an adult policyholder`)

-- 11.1(b): 89 days abroad and no change of work: not this clause; 90 days: it applies.
#ASSERT `11.1(b) — the Company's options on` (`A change under Article 11.1(b)` OF FALSE, 89, TRUE, YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `Article 11.1(b) does not apply`
#ASSERT `11.1(b) — the Company's options on` (`A change under Article 11.1(b)` OF FALSE, 90, FALSE, YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `cover continues unchanged`
#ASSERT `11.1(b) — the Company's options on` (`A change under Article 11.1(b)` OF FALSE, 90, TRUE, YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `the Company may change the premium or sum insured, exclude benefits or terminate, from` (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `11.1(b) — the Company's options on` (`A change under Article 11.1(b)` OF TRUE, 0, TRUE, YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `the Company may change the premium or sum insured, exclude benefits or terminate, from` (YMD 2027 1 1)
